  "title": "Mission tests fail under load: start status and cancel race",
  "objective": "Two CR-2026-0123 mission tests pass alone but fail under load (full `just test`, or a run's validation gate). They have failed several gates, including run-18d93c056079b9c0 and a local `just test` on 2026-09-27.\n\nDiagnosis so far (from reading the code; confirm before changing anything):\n\n1. `mission_routes_enforce_records_revisions_messages_and_controls` (crates/spark-http/tests/contracts/workspace_route_contracts.rs:667) builds the app with `QuietAgent`, whose turns finish immediately, then asserts status `running` right after `POST /start`. Status is derived on read, so when the stub turn has already finished, `needs_you` is correct. Test defect. Fix: use a gated agent like `GatedAgent` in crates/spark-workspace/tests/contracts/mission_contracts.rs so the first turn is in flight when status is asserted, then release it and assert `needs_you`. Do not weaken assertions.\n\n2. `cancel_stops_owned_runs_and_closes_the_mission` (crates/spark-workspace/tests/contracts/mission_contracts.rs) relies on a `sleep 3` tool still running when it cancels; under load the cancel can arrive after the run reaches its final node. Test fix: replace the sleep with the repo's release-file gate pattern (commit 978530bf, 'Make the webhook dispatch contract load-independent'): the tool blocks until the test creates a file, released only after the cancel is asserted.\n\n3. Product gap behind (2): the executor (crates/attractor-runtime/src/executor.rs) checks for cancel only between nodes, and the final completed write uses its in-memory record, so a cancel accepted during the last node is silently overwritten as `completed`. Fix at the root: immediately before finalizing as completed, re-read the run record and finalize as canceled if it is `cancel_requested`. Add a regression test for a cancel during the final node.\n\nDone when both tests are deterministic under a loaded full `just test` (run it several times), and the executor honours a cancel accepted before completion, with a regression test.",
